From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -rb_ports, banked read ports

-rb_ports n adds n banked read ports to a RAM with -banks: each has an
address and a data output per bank (addr_rb<k>_b<b>, Qrb<k>_b<b>), the
address the word's index in its bank, every bank read independently in
the same cycle, as XiangShan's integer register file reads. To the
generator below, each (port, bank) is a read port of its own that
decodes and reads only its bank's words: a tristate bitline or an
AND-OR tree over them. The behavioral model reads the same words.

The sixth of the generate_regfile features carried onto generate_ram;
see OpenROAD #11669. Not upstreamed.

---
